I found a spellbook called "finger of death".  Sounded really cool to
me.  When I ran into a minotaur I decided to try it.  I immediately
goofed it up and couldn't remember the spell...even though it was
my first time.  BTW, wisdom and intelligence are both at 18.
What is finger of death and will I be able to use it?  Anyone?

Now for an idea that came to mind today (probably after thinking
about finger of death).  How about the "Midas touch"?  Either in
spellbook form, potion, or a dead monster.  Of course, everything
you touch would turn to gold.  Of course this would
be a blessing as much as a curse.  Thoughts on it:

1. your weilded weapon would automatically turn to gold which would
   make it rust proof and resistant to corrosion but would also make
   it VERY heavy.   Same thing if you touched your armor.

2. If you touched stones they would become gold pieces.

3. If you touched a monster it would turn to gold...perhaps by
   applying your pick-axe you could then chip the statue into
   gold pieces.  Of course then your pick axe would turn to gold.

Has this been thought of before?  Thoughts anyone?

